# Baseline run side effects: logs, checkpoints, per-step traces.
runs/

# Unpublished methods are now tracked rather than ignored, so that a
# refactor of the shared protocol can be reviewed against every
# baseline that implements it rather than against the public half.
#
# What used to be enforced here -- that the code could not be committed
# -- is enforced at the other end instead, by a pre-push hook that
# refuses to publish these paths or the method's name. The hook is not
# tracked, because naming the method in a tracked file is the thing
# being prevented. It lives in .git/hooks/pre-push; a fresh clone does
# not get it, so install it before adding a remote.
#
# Pushing anything at all is blocked while these files are tracked:
# a push publishes whole trees, not diffs, so any descendant commit
# would carry them. Strip them from history before publishing.
#
# Results still stay out: artefact paths carry the algorithm's name,
# and nothing about a run needs to be in git.
benchmarks/**/private/
benchmarks/private/
runs/**/private/
runs/private/
